    <string name="guide_title">Wireless Debugging Setup Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_step_1_title">1. Enable Developer Options</string>
    <string name="guide_step_1_desc">Go to Android Settings &gt; About Phone. Tap \'Build Number\' 7 times until Developer Options are unlocked.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_2_title">2. Enable Wireless Debugging</string>
    <string name="guide_step_2_desc">Open Settings &gt; System &gt; Developer Options. Turn on \'Wireless debugging\' and connect to a Wi-Fi network.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_3_title">3. Pair Device in Shizuku</string>
    <string name="guide_step_3_desc">Open the Shizuku app, tap \'Pairing\', then switch to Developer Options &gt; \'Pair device with pairing code\'. Enter the 6-digit code in the Shizuku notification.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_4_title">4. Start Shizuku Service</string>
    <string name="guide_step_4_desc">Return to Shizuku and tap \'Start\'. Shizuku will start running in ADB shell mode (UID 2000).</string>

    <string name="quirks_title">OEM Specific Quirks &amp; Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="quirk_xiaomi_title">Xiaomi / HyperOS / MIUI</string>
    <string name="quirk_xiaomi_desc">You must enable \'USB debugging (Security settings)\' under Developer Options. This requires inserting a SIM card and logging into a Mi account once.</string>
    <string name="quirk_oppo_title">OPPO / Realme / OnePlus (ColorOS)</string>
    <string name="quirk_oppo_desc">Disable \'Permission monitoring\' or \'Disable permission monitoring\' switch in Developer Options to prevent ColorOS from revoking ADB permissions.</string>
    <string name="quirk_reboot_title">Device Reboot Notice</string>
    <string name="quirk_reboot_desc">Android system kills Shizuku processes when your device restarts. Simply open Shizuku and tap Start via Wireless Debugging again (no PC needed!).</string>

